Er, definitely not.

In German, the definite article mutates dependent on case, number, and
gender.  In English, it never mutates (it is always "the").

English is in general an ungendered language (or functionally so).
German has three genders.

Regular English verbs have exactly two distinct present-tense endings
(unless you're using archaic English forms).  German has at least five.

OTOH I believe German word order is rather stricter.

